The fifth module for Parallel 2.0 has been released today, 20 January
2006. It has 179 pairs of English-Lojban sentences and 1.85 MB, or 16
minutes, of low-quality sound. It also features the famous "All Your Base Are
Belong To Us" phrase.
Download from attachments here:
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Parallel%202

The next, sixth, module will be the last one inspired by "Lojban For
Beginners" lessons. After that I start the project to create examples
for all gismu and cmavo existing so far (1-5 examples per each). The examples will be wrapped
in the same Parallel Module format as before, complete with sound.
That is VERY ambitious, and many ambitious projects fail.
I would like to know if someone can help me in creating examples and
recording sound for them.

mi'e .ianis.



